artifacts/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.DS_Store
# keys live here and nowhere else in the tree
.env
# working copies of previous runs, kept on disk to compare against. The committed state is
# whichever corpus data/frozen.json binds the query sets to; the rest is history, not source.
.backup-*/
# the ingest cache: 39 MB, and `make corpus` regenerates it. What must be committed is
# data/corpus.jsonl (the frozen subset the query sets are bound to by sha), not its source.
data/raw/
# downloaded MSMARCO-XI shards: gigabytes each, and `make corpus` fetches them on demand
data/shards/
# the clips are yours and are not committed; the note saying what to record is
data/audio/*
!data/audio/README.md

# The corpus is now a build artifact, not source. At 1,200 docs it was 17 MB and committing
# it made the repo reproducible in one clone; at 30,000 it is 515 MB, past what GitHub will
# take in a single file. `make corpus` regenerates it, every report stamps the corpus sha it
# was measured against, and the frozen query sets that bind to that sha are still committed
# -- so what is checked in is still enough to detect a mismatch, just not to avoid a rebuild.
data/corpus.jsonl
data/msmarco_queries.jsonl

# the MSMARCO-XI train shards: 3.7 GB each, and the ingest samples a few thousand rows
# from them. What belongs in the repo is the frozen sample, not the quarry it came from.
training data/
